<title>ZAMBIA: Zambian treasury bill rates drop slightly in April.</title>
<headline>Zambian treasury bill rates drop slightly in April.</headline>
<dateline>LUSAKA 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zambia's treasury bill rates dropped slightly in April, the central bank said.</p>
<p>It said yield rates for 28 and 91-day treasury bills, for the fortnight ending April 18, fell by 1.9 and 1.4 percentage points respectively to 30.3 and 34.8 percent.</p>
<p>The yield on the 182-day treasury bills fell by 2.5 percentage points to 35.6 percent.</p>
<p>-- Lusaka newsroom +2601 222 689</p>
</text>
